bin/
*.log
whitepaper.pdf
docker/build/
docker/run/

# Android native libraries, fetched by make android-deps (29MB+).
android/libs/

# Built by make aar (18MB).
android/*.aar
.gradle-cache/
android/app/build/
android/.gradle/
android/*.apk
android/*-sources.jar
android/shrooms-unsigned.apk
android/.kotlin/

# The decision record, rendered from docs/adr/*.md by scripts/render-adrs.py
# (make site-adrs). Not committed: the markdown is the source, the Pages
# workflow builds these on every deploy, and a checked-in copy is twenty-seven
# files that go stale the moment somebody edits an ADR without running the
# renderer.
site/adr/

# Prose rendered from docs/*.md by the same script, into site/ rather than
# site/adr/. Same reason: the markdown is the source and a checked-in copy goes
# stale the moment somebody edits the markdown without running the renderer.
site/comparison.html

# nix build outputs: symlinks into /nix/store, valid on exactly one machine.
# They were committed by accident and are pure churn — every rebuild changes
# them, and the target does not exist for anybody who clones this.
/result
/result-core

# built by `make relay`.
#
# Anchored, because a bare `shrooms-relay` matches any path component of that
# name — including the cmd/shrooms-relay directory, whose sources then silently
# never got committed. CI failed for fifteen commits on an undefined function
# that was plainly defined, while every local build worked because the files
# were on disk.
/shrooms-relay

# Runtime store from the rendezvous library.
#
# The library resolves storeMessageDbUrl against the working directory, so a
# daemon or a test run from the repository root writes its message store here.
# It was committed once by an over-broad `git add -A` — 32 MB of it — and then
# broke every later commit with "confused by unstable object source data",
# because a running node was writing to the file git was hashing.
data/

# Built by hand with `go build -o shrooms ./cmd/shrooms`. The Makefile writes
# bin/shrooms, which the first line of this file already ignores — this is the
# stray that gets left in the working tree by a build run without -o.
#
# Anchored, for the reason /shrooms-relay is: a bare `shrooms` would also match
# the cmd/shrooms directory and silently stop its sources being committed.
#
# It reached nine commits before anybody noticed, 13 MB each time, always as a
# passenger in a feature commit rather than on purpose — the same over-broad
# `git add -A` that put data/ in here. The copy that was tracked reported its
# version as "dev", so it was never a release artifact either.
/shrooms

# Built by `make dist` (scripts/build-portable.sh), which regenerates the tree
# from packaging/ and the library Basecamp installed.
#
# Committed once with the installer and then carried as 50 MB of generated
# output. Every part of it has a tracked source: dist/install.sh is a
# byte-identical copy of packaging/install-dist.sh, and dist/lib/*.so are
# byte-identical to docker/build/lib, which this file already ignores.
#
# Nothing reads it from the repository — the build script excludes dist/ from
# its own context, and CI builds the tree itself and uploads it as an artifact.
# A checked-in copy only goes stale, which is the reason site/adr and
# docker/build are ignored above.
dist/
